# What the proxy component keeps out of the repository.
#
# The proxy is a Maven project, so `target/` is its build output and the launcher's working
# directory is the one it is started from -- which, in a checkout, is this directory.

### Build output ###
/target/
/dist/

### Local runtime state ###
# The relay's own working directory: per-run event logs, the generated route table, the install
# manifest, the dashboard's port hint and the claims a running relay learned. All regenerable.
/work/
/logs/

# Written next to the jar by the launcher. Both are artifacts: relay-routes.json is extracted from
# the bundled template, and drelay.jar is the build output of build.ps1 or Maven. (The template
# itself lives in src/main/resources/, which these root-anchored rules do not match.)
/relay-routes.json
/drelay.jar
/drelay-*.jar
/drelay-update.log
